course: dictionary
lesson: 5754
title: Lowland
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lowland is flat land that is low, not much higher than the sea. Read the words around the word to work out what it means. «Most people live in fairly small parts of the land: river valleys, coastal plains and fertile lowlands» tells you that people settle on low, flat land.
explain: Lowlands are often compared with highlands and mountains. «Deserts, high mountains and polar lands are nearly empty» shows that high, rough land has fewer people. Lowlands are the opposite: low, flat and easier to farm and build on.
explain: The word can also name a place. (The Lowlands) are the southern and central part of Scotland, which is lower than the Highlands. As an adjective, lowland describes things, such as lowland farms or lowland rivers.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «They crowd into river valleys, coastal plains and fertile lowlands» still makes sense if you think "low, flat land". That is a good sign that you have the right meaning.
fact: A lowland is flat land that is low, not much higher than the sea.
fact: «Lowlands» can also mean the southern and central part of Scotland, which is lower than the Highlands.
fact: Lowlands are often good for farming and towns, but they can flood.
fact: «Many Maya cities in the southern lowlands declined around 800 to 900» shows that lowlands can be home to people and cities for a long time.
fact: As an adjective, lowland describes things found in low, flat land, such as «lowland farms» and «lowland rivers».
exercise: Which kind of land is a lowland? | Icy land near the poles | High, rocky mountains with snow on top | *Flat land that is low, not much higher than the sea | Dry, empty desert with no rivers
exercise: In geography, what is «the Lowlands» of Scotland compared with? | The volcanoes of Italy | The islands far out at sea | The deserts of Egypt | *The Highlands
exercise: Find and copy the word that names high land in «deserts, high mountains and polar lands are nearly empty». | deserts | empty | nearly | *mountains
test: In geography, lowlands are compared with what? | Oceans and seas | *Highlands and mountains | Deserts and jungles | Rivers and lakes
test: Why can lowlands be a risk for people? | They are too high for farms | They have no rivers at all | They are always covered in ice | *They can flood
exam: Which phrase uses lowland as an adjective? | The desert is hot and dry | Mountains are very tall and steep | The Highlands are cold and windy | *lowland rivers flow gently to the sea
